[{:db/id 17592186096676 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3b6c17fd-0ff9-5d87-b06b-efe5f60e73d4" "question-fdddf3b8-a8e2-50b7-b535-a38f81b62fbd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096463 :question/problem "Luisa has an overdraft facility authorized by her bank. Her bank balance on Monday was $\\[math] 173.25.$ On Tuesday, Luisa decided to withdraw $\\[/math] 250.70$ to buy a laptop. What is Luisa's bank balance at the end of the day on Tuesday?" :question/worked-solution "To find Luisa's bank balance at the end of the day on Tuesday, we subtract the amount of money Luisa spent on the laptop from the starting balance, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\[math] 173.25 - \\[/math] 250.70 = -\\[math] 77.45\n$$\n\nTherefore, Luisa's bank balance at the end of the day on Tuesday was $-\\[/math] 77.45.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096677 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-eee9ef15-a1f2-573e-9281-9406377c6d0e" "question-1b039dc7-fa95-5b45-bb27-8c6ed8ecbe43"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096464 :question/problem "Nazareth is doing an experiment in her Chemistry class. She heated a liquid whose initial temperature was $-5.6^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}.$ After several minutes, the temperature of the liquid rose by $4.7^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C},$ at which point she decided to end the experiment. What was the final temperature of the liquid?" :question/worked-solution "To determine the final temperature of the liquid, we add the change in temperature to the initial temperature of the liquid. This gives\n\n$$\n-5.6^{\\circ}\\,\\textrm{C} + 4.7^{\\circ}\\,\\textrm{C} = -0.9^{\\circ}\\,\\textrm{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the temperature of the liquid at the end of the experiment was $-0.9^{\\circ}\\,\\textrm{C}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096678 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-90030a66-0035-58a4-bb92-3cb6359f5340" "question-090aa86c-d0e1-50e4-9098-0d31886c4162" "question-bea699ae-050c-5792-a06d-737fb3226f50"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096465 :question/worked-solution "To calculate the difference between the elevations of both cities, we must calculate the difference between the city with the highest elevation and the city with the lowest elevation. That is, we must calculate $83.2 - (-52.5).$ This gives\n\n$$\n83.2 - (-52.5) = 83.2 + 52.5 = 135.7 \\, \\textrm{ft}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096679 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-241ae34a-170c-5ddb-b291-a82fcffae551" "question-7e4b7794-21eb-5f19-b665-c965b7cd7892"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096466 :question/problem "In Chicago, the average temperature in December is $-1.5^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}.$ Then in January, the average temperature decreases by $3.5^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$ compared to December. Finally, in February, the average temperature increases by $2.6^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$ compared to the previous month. What is Chicago's average temperature in February?" :question/worked-solution "First, we must determine the temperature in Chicago during the month of January. Since we are told that the temperature *decreases* on average $3.5^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$ compared to December, we *subtract* the variation in temperature from the average temperature in December. This gives\n\n$$\n-1.5^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C} - 3.5^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C} = -5.0^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}.\n$$\n\nNow we must determine the temperature during the month of February. Since we are told that the temperature *increases* on average $2.6^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$ compared to January, we *add* the variation in temperature to the average temperature of January. This gives\n\n$$\n-5.0^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C} + 2.6^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C} = -2.4^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average temperature in Chicago in the month of February is $-2.4^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-3b6c17fd-0ff9-5d87-b06b-efe5f60e73d4" :question/id #uuid "3b6c17fd-0ff9-5d87-b06b-efe5f60e73d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-72687" :question/problem "The average temperature in the Arctic in December of a particular year was ${3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ Due to plummeting temperatures in the winter, the average temperature in February of the next year decreased by ${6.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to the average temperature in December. What was the average temperature in the Arctic in February?" :question/worked-solution "To determine the average temperature of the Arctic in February, we subtract the change in temperature (from December to February) from the average temperature in December. This gives\n\n$$\n{3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}-{6.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}=-{3.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the average temperature in the Arctic at the end of February was $-{3.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-371b26ec-2142-5e84-b536-237d3573a131"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-371b26ec-2142-5e84-b536-237d3573a131" :answer-field/id #uuid "371b26ec-2142-5e84-b536-237d3573a131" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-56c45950-130f-53fe-a976-47b21989b82b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4a5ecfb1-81e3-578f-8bc4-593731a199e8" "answer-dfa1c13a-b211-59e8-af4d-7dcb692be74c" "answer-4ca87e66-4ef9-5a01-9d25-9e7126c88980" "answer-56c45950-130f-53fe-a976-47b21989b82b" "answer-09c7887f-43ee-5006-a75e-672b5588253f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a5ecfb1-81e3-578f-8bc4-593731a199e8" :answer/id #uuid "4a5ecfb1-81e3-578f-8bc4-593731a199e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{2.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfa1c13a-b211-59e8-af4d-7dcb692be74c" :answer/id #uuid "dfa1c13a-b211-59e8-af4d-7dcb692be74c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}" :